:null,"size":null,"optional":false,"aisle":"produce","pantry":false,"shop":true,"one":"fresh parsley"}],"steps":[{"text":"Warm the broth in the small pot and keep it at a bare simmer.","uses":[0]},{"text":"Heat the oil in the large pan over medium-high heat. Cook the mushrooms with half the salt, stirring only occasionally, until browned and their liquid has evaporated, {time 8 min}. Set aside.","uses":[1,2,3]},{"text":"Lower the heat to medium, add 1 tbsp butter and the shallot and cook until soft, {time 3 min}. Add the garlic and rice and stir until the rice edges look translucent, {time 2 min}.","uses":[4,5,6,7]},{"text":"Pour in the wine and stir until absorbed. Add the thyme, the rest of the salt and a ladle of hot broth, and stir until it is almost absorbed.","uses":[8,9]},{"text":"Keep adding broth a ladle at a time, stirring often, until the rice is tender with a slight bite and the risotto flows like thick porridge, {time 18-22 min}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Stir in the mushrooms, the remaining butter and the cheese off the heat. Add a splash more broth to loosen it, cover and rest for {time 2 min}. Serve with parsley.","uses":[10,11]}]}